            <ArticleTitle>Cardiovascular drugs and exercise interactions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An appreciation of the hemodynamic and biochemical changes induced by drugs is critical for a logical diagnostic interpretation of graded stress tests and the evaluation of the projected exercise prescription and exercise programs that a patient is asked to follow. Drug therapy is clearly not a contraindication to acute or chronic exercise as long as the potential benefits and complications of exercise and drug interaction are considered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
